; root cluster for the IS-A classification system.
; taxonomy is the grammar of kinds — what IS a kind of what.
; this is the structural ground for syllogism and categorical inference.
; 
; in the proof graph, IS-A is the swarupa edge.
; "cat is a mammal" = [cat, swarupa, mammal]
; "mammal is an animal" = [mammal, swarupa, animal]
; walking the swarupa chain from cat reaches animal — this IS anumana.
; 
; properties (yukta edges) are inherited along the swarupa chain.
; if animal has breathing-yukta, and cat has mammal-swarupa and mammal has
; animal-swarupa, then cat inherits breathing through the chain.
; the anumana-viveka tantra walks this structure at query time.
; 
; this mirrors how biology-varga, cell-varga, genetics-varga form
; a classification within the biology domain — except taxonomy applies
; to common-sense kinds before formal domains take over.
; sangati roots for the classification act itself

(kosha taxonomy-varga
  (sthita domain-common-sense)
  (vishesa common-sense-varga)
  (swarupa subanta)
  (yukta swarupa krama viveka))
